                <pb facs="0463" n="451" sameAs="frus:frus1942v05/pg451"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20(D) E.D.B./1789: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-10-07T17:00:00-04:00">October 7, 1942—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1503. Embassy’s A–196, September 16. The Department is informed that six drums
                    are being shipped for the Standard Oil Company of New Jersey.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
